      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are 5 rewritten behavioral interview questions that explicitly incorporate the core terms from your culture deck, while staying conversational and usable:\n\n1. Can you walk me through how you navigated the iterative process of ideation and prototyping in a recent project? How did you leverage the diverse perspectives of your team to drive innovative solutions and foster collaboration?\n2. Tell a story about a complex problem you encountered in your previous role. How did you approach it with a growth-mindset, seeking out the input and expertise of your team to drive breakthroughs and achieve synergy?\n3. Describe a situation where you and your team had to pivot to address a project delay or setback. How did you facilitate open communication and collaboration to identify mutually beneficial solutions that ultimately drove innovation and team success?\n4. How do you handle conflicting priorities and feedback from stakeholders in a collaborative work environment? Can you give an example of a time when you employs inclusive decision-making principles or served as a team leader to drive shared results?\n5. In what ways do you strive for continuous improvement and synergy within your team? Can you share a specific instance where adopting a horizontal mindset (e.g., collaborating instead of hierarchically-managing) or driving a high-growth scenario (e",
